  {
   "kind": "fact",
   "text": "Bubble Wrap was first meant to be wallpaper. In 1957, two inventors sealed shower curtains together with air trapped inside, but the 3D wall covering didn't catch on.",
   "topic": "inventions",
   "note": "The company that makes Bubble Wrap, Sealed Air, confirmed this story to HuffPost. The material was first used to pack IBM computers.",
   "sources": [
    {
     "url": "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/bubble-wrap-wallpaper_n_56a65965e4b0404eb8f24f6d",
     "title": "Turns Out Bubble Wrap Was Originally Meant To Be Wallpaper",
     "publisher": "HuffPost"
    },
    {
